    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365-a5">

                <pb facs="0383" n="1061" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1061"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 131.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 2, 1862—10 <hi rendition="#italic">o’clock p.
                            m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have just had an interview with a
                    governor of foreign affairs, and he assures me that the Japanese government have
                    taken every precaution to insure the safety of the seamen and property of the
                    American ship which has been wrecked, and that every assistance will be
                    rendered, and all needful protection given to its crew and our consul,</p>
                <p>I avail myself, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United
                            States in Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Duchesne de Bellecourt</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">His Imperial Majesty’s Minister Plenipotentiary in
                            Japan.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
